'' ===========================================================================
''
''   File.......  test-contract-gaps-p2-cog-lifecycle.spin2
''   Purpose....  Seven cog-lifecycle and data questions, arms I to O, each
''                with controls that must come out both ways.  Pins P0..P2.
''   Manual.....  P2 Knowledge Base
''   Authors....  Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail.....  stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started....  Nov 2026
''   Updated....  Nov 2026
''
'' ===========================================================================

{ RIG
  Bare P2 board, 200 MHz, NOTHING attached.  Pins touched: P0..P2 only.
  Build pnut-ts -d.  Cog 0 supervises and prints; no other cog has the
  debugger.  Every step runs in a worker cog that writes its record to hub
  and DONE last; the supervisor stops a worker that has not finished in its
  limit and reports the step as hung.  Results print before verdicts.

ARM I  What survives COGINIT of a running cog, of a stopped cog, and of
  itself?  One image is both the reader and the dirtier.  The reader's first
  instructions capture: a skip detector (eight ADDs), C, Z, PA, PB, Q (MUXQ),
  a REP detector (an ADD at $010 inside a three-instruction block), DIRA,
  OUTA, a LUT long, eight POPs, and the CT1 event over a 5 ms window.
    Baseline     the reader started in cog 7, never used since boot.
    Dirty        DIR %011, OUT %101 on P0..P2, C = Z = 1, eight pushes, PA,
                 PB, Q, a LUT long, CT1 due 2 ms ahead.  Skip: a pattern with
                 pending 1s held by a SKIP loop.  REP: a REP over $010..$012.
    Scenarios    the dirty cog restarted by cog 0 while running; stopped by
                 cog 0, then restarted; restarting itself.
    Control      the dirtier jumps into its own reader with no COGINIT: every
                 class must read dirty.  For REP the jump lands on the REP
                 instruction, since a branch inside a REP block cancels it.
  Each class reads SURVIVES (= dirty, not baseline), RESET (= baseline, not
  dirty), INCONCLUSIVE (baseline = dirty) or OTHER.  PA and PB sit in the
  loaded range $000..$1F7, so their baseline is the image's own longs.  The
  stack compares all eight pops; CT1 compares a form: fired within 200 clocks
  of the dirty target, never fired, set at the reader's start, or fired at
  another time.  A stack SURVIVES cannot tell a surviving stack pointer from
  surviving stack RAM, since the 8-deep stack wraps.
    Premises     cog 0 restarts or stops a running dirty cog 100 us after it
                 reports ready.  The skip loop carries a heartbeat and an ADD
                 on a pending 1-bit: the heartbeat must be moving and the
                 ADD's count still 0; the self-restart runs the same canary
                 just before its COGINIT.  The REP block writes its count to
                 hub on every pass (a REP of 1,000,000 passes, about 100 ms):
                 the count must be moving, and the REP must not have run out
                 first.  The self-restart's REP is five instructions that pass
                 once with the COGINIT cancelled, so a second pass, which only
                 the REP brings, writes 2 and runs the COGINIT; the last count
                 must be 2.  A missing premise makes that scenario a RIG FAIL.

ARM J  Is a cog's OUT gated by its own DIR?  P0, read three times.
    Controls     cog 0 DIR 1 OUT 0 alone reads 0; a worker DIR 1 OUT 1 alone
                 reads 1; a worker DIR 1 OUT 0 alone reads 0; cog 0 DIR 1
                 OUT 1 alone reads 1.
    Measure      cog 0 DIR 1 OUT 0 with a worker DIR 0 OUT 1; then swapped.
                 1 = INDEPENDENT, 0 = GATED.

ARM K  Which read retires a CORDIC result?  QMUL k,$FFFF_FFFF gives
  X = -k, Y = k - 1, so each value names its k.  Two results queued (k 3, 5).
    Controls     four GETQX after four QMULs read k 3, 5, 7, 9 in order;
                 GETQY then GETQX twice reads Y3 X3 Y5 X5.
    Measure      GETQX twice, GETQX then GETQY, GETQY twice: the second read
                 names k 5 (RETIRED) or k 3 (NOT RETIRED).

ARM L  What does QDIV return when the quotient exceeds 32 bits?
    Controls     1000 / 3 = 333 r 1; {1,0} / 4 = $4000_0000 r 0; a divide by
                 zero with {$1234_5678, 7} gives NOT $1234_5678 r 7.
    Measure      {3,7} / 2 and {5,11} / 4: WRAP ($8000_0003, $4000_0002, the
                 low 32 bits), SATURATE ($FFFF_FFFF), or OTHER; the remainder
                 against the true remainder.
    Premise      without its SETQ each divide would give 3 r 1 and 2 r 3;
                 either quotient seen means the high long is not shown.

ARM M  What does GETQX return with nothing pending, and in how many clocks?
    Controls     a back-to-back GETCT pair reads its 2-clock overhead; a
                 GETQX with a QMUL pending waits, returns the result and
                 leaves the empty flag clear.
    Measure      two empty reads, each after a different result: the value
                 (STALE = the last result, ZERO, or OTHER) and the clocks;
                 the empty flag must be set.

ARM N  The unit of RDLUT / WRLUT PTRA indexes and updates.  LUT[i] =
  $C0DE_0000 + i, PTRA = 8.
    Controls     a plain RDLUT reads its long; RDLONG PTRA[2] and PTRA++ on a
                 hub long array step by 4; RDBYTE on a byte array steps by 1.
    Measure      RDLUT PTRA[2] index read; RDLUT PTRA++ index and delta;
                 WRLUT PTRA++ index written and delta.  LONGS or TIMES 4.

ARM O  CRCNIB's bit order.  CRC 0, polynomial $8C, nibbles %1000 and %1101.
    Control      four CRCBITs fed Q[31] down and fed Q[28] up must differ.
    Measure      CRCNIB equals the down order (Q[31] FIRST) or the up order.

NOT MEASURED
  COGINIT that starts without loading (D[5] = 1), PTRA/PTRB, events other
  than CT1, the LUT beyond one long, interrupts; other CORDIC operations; LUT
  PTRB and the -- forms.  One part, N = 1.
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq        = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_COGS      = %0000_0001

  REC_N           = 32
  R_DONE          = 0
  R_MODE          = 1
  R_P1            = 2
  R_P2            = 3
  R_V             = 4                   ' first result long
  DONE_V          = $0D0E_0D0E
  SENT            = $5E5E_5E5E
  STEP_MS         = 50

  ' ---- arm I ----
  I_READY         = 4                   ' the dirtier sets this when its state is in place
  I_TD            = 5                   ' the CT1 target the dirtier set
  I_CAP           = 6                   ' first of the captured longs
  I_NCAP          = 22
  IR_BEAT          = 28                  ' the skip loop's heartbeat
  IR_LEAK          = 29                  ' 0 while the skip pattern cancels its pending ADD
  COG_BASE        = 7                   ' never used before arm I
  COG_TEST        = 6
  READY_MS        = 100
  READ_MS         = 300
  HOLD_US         = 100                 ' after READY, before cog 0 restarts or stops the cog
  SC_RUN          = 0
  SC_STOP         = 1
  SC_SELF         = 2
  SC_JMP          = 3
  V_PAS           = 1                   ' dirty variants: passive state, skip, REP
  V_SKIP          = 2
  V_REP           = 3
  K_CTL           = 10                  ' REP count of the plain-jump control
  K_SELF          = 20                  ' REP count around the self COGINIT
  K_BIG           = 1_000_000           ' REP count held while cog 0 restarts the cog
  CT_DEL          = 400_000             ' CT1 target 2 ms ahead
  CT_WIN          = 1_000_000           ' the reader watches CT1 for 5 ms
  CT_TOL          = 200
  I_LS            = $0F0                ' the LUT long
  D_DIR           = %011
  D_OUT           = %101
  D_PA            = $DA00_00A1
  D_PB            = $DA00_00B1
  D_Q             = $DA00_0051
  D_LUT           = $DA00_0071
  D_STK           = $5A00_0000          ' pushes D_STK + 1 .. D_STK + 8
  IMG_PA          = $1A6E_00A1          ' the image's longs at $1F6, $1F7
  IMG_PB          = $1A6E_00B1
  C_SKM           = 0                   ' capture indexes
  C_CV            = 1
  C_ZV            = 2
  C_PA            = 3
  C_PB            = 4
  C_Q             = 5
  C_RPC           = 6
  C_DIR           = 7
  C_OUT           = 8
  C_LUT           = 9
  C_ST0           = 10
  C_CT0           = 18
  C_CTFL          = 19
  C_CTF           = 20
  C_CTST          = 21

  ' ---- arm J ----
  J_PIN           = 0
  J_READY         = R_V
  J_STATE         = R_V + 1             ' the worker's DIR | OUT << 1, read back

  ' ---- arms K to O ----
  M_KX4           = 0
  M_KYX           = 1
  M_KXX           = 2
  M_KXY           = 3
  M_KYY           = 4
  M_L             = 5
  M_M             = 6
  M_N             = 7
  M_O             = 8
  LUTBASE         = $C0DE_0000
  N_MARK          = $3A4B_5C6D

VAR ' ---- Rig State ----
  long  rec[REC_N]
  long  recD[REC_N]                     ' the dirtier's record
  long  recR[REC_N]                     ' the reader's record
  long  ib[I_NCAP]                      ' arm I baseline
  long  ic[I_NCAP]                      ' arm I plain-jump control
  long  irn[I_NCAP]                     ' arm I running
  long  ist[I_NCAP]                     ' arm I stopped
  long  isl[I_NCAP]                     ' arm I itself
  long  tdc, tdr, tds, tdl              ' CT1 targets: control, running, stopped, itself
  long  okc, okr, oks, okl              ' each scenario finished
  long  dirtyDone                       ' the dirtier finished its own REP before the restart
  long  skipHeld                        ' the skip pattern or REP was shown in place at the restart
  long  hr, hs, hl                      ' skipHeld for running, stopped, itself
  long  outR, outS                      ' dirtyDone for running, stopped

PUB main()
'' Run arms I to O and print every reading and verdict.
''

  p0(string("=== test-contract-gaps-p2-cog-lifecycle ==="))
  arm_i()
  arm_j()
  arm_k()
  arm_l()
  arm_m()
  arm_n()
  arm_o()
  p0(string("=== END ==="))
  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat

PRI launch(pImg, mode, p1v, p2v) : ok | cog, t0
' Run one step in a fresh worker cog and wait for its DONE.
'
' @param pImg - hub address of the worker image
' @param mode - the step number
' @param p1v - first hub address the step needs
' @param p2v - second hub address the step needs
' @returns ok - TRUE when the worker wrote DONE in time

' Local Variables:
' @local cog - the worker cog
' @local t0 - CT at the launch

  longfill(@rec, SENT, REC_N)
  rec[R_DONE] := 0
  rec[R_MODE] := mode
  rec[R_P1] := p1v
  rec[R_P2] := p2v
  cog := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, pImg, @rec)
  if cog < 0
    p0(string("RIG FAIL: no free cog for a step"))
    return FALSE
  t0 := getct()
  repeat until rec[R_DONE] == DONE_V
    if getct() - t0 > clkfreq / 1000 * STEP_MS
      cogstop(cog)
      p1(string("STEP HUNG: no DONE within the step limit, mode"), mode)
      return FALSE
  cogstop(cog)
  ok := TRUE

PRI wait_for(pRec, idx, value, ms) : ok | t0
' Wait until a record long holds a value.
'
' @param pRec - the record
' @param idx - the long's index
' @param value - the value to wait for
' @param ms - the limit
' @returns ok - TRUE when it arrived in time

  t0 := getct()
  repeat until long[pRec][idx] == value
    if getct() - t0 > clkfreq / 1000 * ms
      return FALSE
  ok := TRUE

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm I

PRI i_prep(pRec, mode, p1v)
' Fill a record and set its mode.
'
' @param pRec - the record
' @param mode - 0 to read, or a dirty mode
' @param p1v - the record the restarted reader writes

  longfill(pRec, SENT, REC_N)
  long[pRec][R_DONE] := 0
  long[pRec][R_MODE] := mode
  long[pRec][R_P1] := p1v
  long[pRec][R_P2] := @i_r00
  long[pRec][I_READY] := 0

PRI i_scen(v, sc, pDst) : ok | b1, b2
' Run one scenario of variant v and copy the reader's captures.  Sets
' dirtyDone when the dirty cog finished its own REP before the restart, and
' skipHeld when the skip pattern or the REP was shown in place at the restart.
'
' @param v - V_PAS, V_SKIP or V_REP
' @param sc - SC_RUN, SC_STOP, SC_SELF or SC_JMP
' @param pDst - where the captures go
' @returns ok - TRUE when the reader reported in time

' Local Variables:
' @local b1 - the skip loop's heartbeat before the restart
' @local b2 - the heartbeat 20 us later

  dirtyDone := FALSE
  skipHeld := TRUE
  b1 := SENT
  b2 := SENT
  i_prep(@recR, 0, 0)
  if sc == SC_SELF
    i_prep(@recD, v * 4 + sc, @recR)
  else
    i_prep(@recD, v * 4 + sc, 0)
  coginit(COG_TEST, @i_r00, @recD)
  case sc
    SC_JMP:
      ok := wait_for(@recD, R_DONE, DONE_V, READY_MS + READ_MS)
      longmove(pDst, @recD[I_CAP], I_NCAP)
    SC_SELF:
      ok := wait_for(@recR, R_DONE, DONE_V, READY_MS + READ_MS)
      longmove(pDst, @recR[I_CAP], I_NCAP)
      if v == V_SKIP
        skipHeld := recD[IR_LEAK] == 0
      elseif v == V_REP
        skipHeld := recD[IR_BEAT] == 2  ' the second pass, which only REP brings, ran the COGINIT
    other:
      ok := wait_for(@recD, I_READY, 1, READY_MS)
      if ok
        waitus(HOLD_US)                 ' the dirty cog is inside its loop, REP or skip by now
        if v == V_SKIP or v == V_REP
          b1 := recD[IR_BEAT]
          waitus(20)
          b2 := recD[IR_BEAT]
          skipHeld := b1 <> SENT and b2 <> b1
          if v == V_SKIP
            skipHeld := skipHeld and recD[IR_LEAK] == 0
        if sc == SC_STOP
          cogstop(COG_TEST)
        coginit(COG_TEST, @i_r00, @recR)
        ok := wait_for(@recR, R_DONE, DONE_V, READ_MS)
        dirtyDone := recD[R_DONE] == DONE_V
      longmove(pDst, @recR[I_CAP], I_NCAP)
  if v == V_SKIP and sc <> SC_JMP
    p3(string("I skip premise: heartbeat, 20 us later, leak (0 = pattern cancelling)"), b1, b2, recD[IR_LEAK])
  if v == V_REP and sc <> SC_JMP
    p3(string("I REP premise: count, 20 us later (moving), last count written (2 = the restart ran inside the REP, itself)"), b1, b2, recD[IR_BEAT])
  cogstop(COG_TEST)
  waitms(1)

PRI i_raw(pName, pCap, td)
' Print one scenario's captures.
'
' @param pName - the scenario
' @param pCap - its captures
' @param td - its CT1 target

  p0(pName)
  p4(string("  skip, C, Z, PA"), long[pCap][C_SKM], long[pCap][C_CV], long[pCap][C_ZV], long[pCap][C_PA])
  p4(string("  PB, Q, REP count, DIR"), long[pCap][C_PB], long[pCap][C_Q], long[pCap][C_RPC], long[pCap][C_DIR])
  p4(string("  OUT, LUT, CT1 flag at start, CT1 fired"), long[pCap][C_OUT], long[pCap][C_LUT], long[pCap][C_CT0], long[pCap][C_CTFL])
  p4(string("  CT1 fired at, reader start, target, fired minus target"), long[pCap][C_CTF], long[pCap][C_CTST], td, long[pCap][C_CTF] - td)
  p4(string("  pops 1..4"), long[pCap][C_ST0], long[pCap][C_ST0 + 1], long[pCap][C_ST0 + 2], long[pCap][C_ST0 + 3])
  p4(string("  pops 5..8"), long[pCap][C_ST0 + 4], long[pCap][C_ST0 + 5], long[pCap][C_ST0 + 6], long[pCap][C_ST0 + 7])

PRI stk_form(pCap) : f | i
' The stack class of a capture: 1 the dirty pushes, 2 the baseline's pops, 0 other.
'
' @param pCap - the captures
' @returns f - 1, 2 or 0

  f := 1
  repeat i from 0 to 7
    if long[pCap][C_ST0 + i] <> D_STK + 8 - i
      f := 0
  if f == 0
    f := 2
    repeat i from 0 to 7
      if long[pCap][C_ST0 + i] <> ib[C_ST0 + i]
        f := 0

PRI ct_form(pCap, td) : f
' The CT1 class of a capture: 1 fired at the dirty target, 2 never fired,
' 3 already set when the reader started, 0 fired at another time.
'
' @param pCap - the captures
' @param td - the dirty target
' @returns f - 0..3

  if long[pCap][C_CT0] <> 0
    f := 3
  elseif long[pCap][C_CTFL] == 0
    f := 2
  elseif long[pCap][C_CTF] - td >= 0 and long[pCap][C_CTF] - td <= CT_TOL
    f := 1
  else
    f := 0

PRI i_judge(pScen, pCls, ok, val, bv, dv, ctlOk, pSurv)
' Print one class's verdict for one scenario.
'
' @param pScen - the scenario name
' @param pCls - the class name
' @param ok - the scenario finished
' @param val - its reading
' @param bv - the baseline reading
' @param dv - the dirty value for this scenario
' @param ctlOk - the plain-jump control read this class dirty
' @param pSurv - the SURVIVES text for this class

  if not ctlOk
    pv2(pScen, pCls, string("RIG FAIL, the reader did not see this class on a plain jump"), val)
  elseif not ok
    pv2(pScen, pCls, string("NO READING, the scenario hung"), val)
  elseif bv == dv
    pv2(pScen, pCls, string("INCONCLUSIVE, the baseline equals the dirty value"), val)
  elseif val == dv
    pv2(pScen, pCls, pSurv, val)
  elseif val == bv
    pv2(pScen, pCls, string("RESET to the never-used cog's value"), val)
  else
    pv2(pScen, pCls, string("OTHER, neither baseline nor dirty"), val)

PRI i_passive(pScen, pCap, ok, td, dq)
' Judge the ten passive classes for one scenario.
'
' @param pScen - the scenario name
' @param pCap - its captures
' @param ok - it finished
' @param td - its CT1 target
' @param dq - the dirty Q for this scenario

  i_judge(pScen, string("DIR"), ok, long[pCap][C_DIR], ib[C_DIR], D_DIR, ic[C_DIR] == D_DIR, @sSurv)
  i_judge(pScen, string("OUT"), ok, long[pCap][C_OUT], ib[C_OUT], D_OUT, ic[C_OUT] == D_OUT, @sSurv)
  i_judge(pScen, string("C"), ok, long[pCap][C_CV], ib[C_CV], 1, ic[C_CV] == 1, @sSurv)
  i_judge(pScen, string("Z"), ok, long[pCap][C_ZV], ib[C_ZV], 1, ic[C_ZV] == 1, @sSurv)
  i_judge(pScen, string("stack"), ok, stk_form(pCap), stk_form(@ib), 1, stk_form(@ic) == 1, string("SURVIVES, the eight pops returned the dirty pushes; this cannot tell a surviving stack pointer from surviving stack RAM, since the 8-deep stack wraps"))
  i_judge(pScen, string("PA"), ok, long[pCap][C_PA], ib[C_PA], D_PA, ic[C_PA] == D_PA, @sSurv)
  i_judge(pScen, string("PB"), ok, long[pCap][C_PB], ib[C_PB], D_PB, ic[C_PB] == D_PB, @sSurv)
  i_judge(pScen, string("Q"), ok, long[pCap][C_Q], ib[C_Q], dq, ic[C_Q] == D_Q, @sSurv)
  i_judge(pScen, string("LUT"), ok, long[pCap][C_LUT], ib[C_LUT], D_LUT, ic[C_LUT] == D_LUT, @sSurv)
  i_judge(pScen, string("CT target"), ok, ct_form(pCap, td), ct_form(@ib, 0), 1, ct_form(@ic, tdc) == 1, @sSurv)

PRI arm_i() | okb
' What a COGINIT leaves, for three restarts and three dirty variants.
'

  i_prep(@recR, 0, 0)
  coginit(COG_BASE, @i_r00, @recR)
  okb := wait_for(@recR, R_DONE, DONE_V, READ_MS)
  cogstop(COG_BASE)
  longmove(@ib, @recR[I_CAP], I_NCAP)
  i_raw(string("I baseline, never-used cog"), @ib, 0)
  p3(string("I image PA, PB; baseline finished"), IMG_PA, IMG_PB, okb)
  if not okb
    pv(string("I"), string("NO READING, the baseline reader hung"))
    return

  ' passive classes
  okc := i_scen(V_PAS, SC_JMP, @ic)
  tdc := recD[I_TD]
  okr := i_scen(V_PAS, SC_RUN, @irn)
  tdr := recD[I_TD]
  oks := i_scen(V_PAS, SC_STOP, @ist)
  tds := recD[I_TD]
  okl := i_scen(V_PAS, SC_SELF, @isl)
  tdl := recD[I_TD]
  i_raw(string("I passive, plain jump (control)"), @ic, tdc)
  i_raw(string("I passive, COGINIT of the running cog"), @irn, tdr)
  i_raw(string("I passive, COGINIT of the stopped cog"), @ist, tds)
  i_raw(string("I passive, COGINIT of itself"), @isl, tdl)
  p4(string("I passive finished: control, running, stopped, itself"), okc, okr, oks, okl)
  p2(string("I dirty Q: cog 0 restarts, itself (the SETQ before its own COGINIT)"), D_Q, @recR)
  if not okc
    pv(string("I passive"), string("NO READING, the plain-jump control hung"))
  else
    i_passive(string("I running"), @irn, okr, tdr, D_Q)
    i_passive(string("I stopped"), @ist, oks, tds, D_Q)
    i_passive(string("I itself"), @isl, okl, tdl, @recR)

  ' skip pattern
  okc := i_scen(V_SKIP, SC_JMP, @ic)
  okr := i_scen(V_SKIP, SC_RUN, @irn)
  hr := skipHeld
  oks := i_scen(V_SKIP, SC_STOP, @ist)
  hs := skipHeld
  okl := i_scen(V_SKIP, SC_SELF, @isl)
  hl := skipHeld
  p4(string("I skip detector (255 = nothing skipped): control, running, stopped, itself"), ic[C_SKM], irn[C_SKM], ist[C_SKM], isl[C_SKM])
  p4(string("I skip finished: control, running, stopped, itself"), okc, okr, oks, okl)
  p3(string("I skip pattern shown in place at the restart: running, stopped, itself"), hr, hs, hl)
  p1(string("I skip detector, baseline"), ib[C_SKM])
  if not okc
    pv(string("I skip"), string("NO READING, the plain-jump control hung"))
  elseif ib[C_SKM] <> 255 or ic[C_SKM] >= 255
    pv(string("I skip"), string("RIG FAIL, the baseline skipped something or the plain-jump control skipped nothing"))
  else
    i_skip(string("I running"), okr, hr, irn[C_SKM])
    i_skip(string("I stopped"), oks, hs, ist[C_SKM])
    i_skip(string("I itself"), okl, hl, isl[C_SKM])
    p0(string("  (I itself, skip: the canary shows the pattern cancelling two instructions before the COGINIT; that its later 1-bits were still pending at the COGINIT follows from the pattern loaded, not from a measurement)"))

  ' REP
  okc := i_scen(V_REP, SC_JMP, @ic)
  okr := i_scen(V_REP, SC_RUN, @irn)
  outR := dirtyDone
  hr := skipHeld
  oks := i_scen(V_REP, SC_STOP, @ist)
  outS := dirtyDone
  hs := skipHeld
  okl := i_scen(V_REP, SC_SELF, @isl)
  hl := skipHeld
  p4(string("I REP detector (1 = once): control, running, stopped, itself"), ic[C_RPC], irn[C_RPC], ist[C_RPC], isl[C_RPC])
  p4(string("I REP finished: control, running, stopped, itself"), okc, okr, oks, okl)
  p2(string("I REP ran out before the restart (must be 0): running, stopped"), outR, outS)
  p3(string("I REP shown in place at the restart: running, stopped, itself"), hr, hs, hl)
  p1(string("I REP detector, baseline"), ib[C_RPC])
  if not okc
    pv(string("I REP"), string("NO READING, the plain-jump control hung"))
  elseif ib[C_RPC] <> 1 or ic[C_RPC] <> K_CTL
    pv(string("I REP"), string("RIG FAIL, the baseline was not 1 or the REP control was not 10"))
  else
    i_rep(string("I running"), okr, outR or not hr, irn[C_RPC])
    i_rep(string("I stopped"), oks, outS or not hs, ist[C_RPC])
    i_rep(string("I itself"), okl, not hl, isl[C_RPC])

PRI i_skip(pScen, ok, held, skm)
' Print a skip-pattern verdict.
'
' @param pScen - the scenario
' @param ok - it finished
' @param held - the pattern was shown in place at the restart
' @param skm - the skip detector

  if not ok
    pv2(pScen, string("skip"), string("NO READING, the scenario hung"), skm)
  elseif not held
    pv2(pScen, string("skip"), string("RIG FAIL, the skip pattern was not shown in place at the restart"), skm)
  elseif skm == 255
    pv2(pScen, string("skip"), string("RESET, nothing in the new program was skipped"), skm)
  elseif skm >= 0 and skm < 255
    pv2(pScen, string("skip"), string("SURVIVES, the new program's first instructions were skipped"), skm)
  else
    pv2(pScen, string("skip"), string("OTHER"), skm)

PRI i_rep(pScen, ok, ranOut, rpc)
' Print a REP verdict.
'
' @param pScen - the scenario
' @param ok - it finished
' @param ranOut - the REP was not shown in force at the restart
' @param rpc - the REP detector

  if not ok
    pv2(pScen, string("REP"), string("NO READING, the scenario hung"), rpc)
  elseif ranOut
    pv2(pScen, string("REP"), string("RIG FAIL, the REP was not shown in force at the restart"), rpc)
  elseif rpc == 1
    pv2(pScen, string("REP"), string("RESET, the block ran once"), rpc)
  elseif rpc > 1
    pv2(pScen, string("REP"), string("SURVIVES, the new program repeated the old block"), rpc)
  else
    pv2(pScen, string("REP"), string("OTHER"), rpc)

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm J

PRI c0set(d, o) : st
' Set cog 0's DIR and OUT bits for the test pin and read them back.
'
' @param d - DIR bit
' @param o - OUT bit
' @returns st - DIR | OUT << 1 as read from cog 0's own registers

  org
        testb   o, #0           wc
        outc    #J_PIN
        testb   d, #0           wc
        dirc    #J_PIN
        testb   dira, #J_PIN    wc
        wrc     st
        testb   outa, #J_PIN    wc
        bitc    st, #1
  end

PRI j_step(d0, o0, dw, ow) : r | cog, a, b, c, s0, sw
' Read the test pin three times with cog 0 and an optional worker set.
'
' @param d0 - cog 0 DIR
' @param o0 - cog 0 OUT
' @param dw - worker DIR, or -1 for no worker
' @param ow - worker OUT
' @returns r - the pin, -1 when the three reads differ, -2 when the worker did
'   not start, -3 when a cog's DIR or OUT read back other than set

  r := -2
  c0set(0, 0)
  cog := -1
  if dw >= 0
    longfill(@rec, SENT, REC_N)
    rec[J_READY] := 0
    rec[R_P1] := dw
    rec[R_P2] := ow
    cog := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, @j_entry, @rec)
    if cog < 0
      return
    if not wait_for(@rec, J_READY, 1, STEP_MS)
      cogstop(cog)
      return
  r := -1
  s0 := c0set(d0, o0)
  waitus(100)
  a := pinread(J_PIN)
  waitus(100)
  b := pinread(J_PIN)
  waitus(100)
  c := pinread(J_PIN)
  sw := (cog >= 0) ? rec[J_STATE] : -1
  if cog >= 0
    cogstop(cog)
  c0set(0, 0)
  waitus(100)
  if s0 <> (d0 | o0 << 1) or (cog >= 0 and sw <> (dw | ow << 1))
    r := -3
  elseif a == b and b == c
    r := a

PRI arm_j() | j1, j2, j3, j4, j5, j6
' Whether a cog's OUT reaches the pin without its own DIR.
'

  pinclear(0 addpins 2)                 ' clear what arm I left on P0..P2
  wrpin(J_PIN, 0)
  j1 := j_step(1, 0, -1, 0)
  j2 := j_step(0, 0, 1, 1)
  j3 := j_step(1, 0, 0, 1)
  j4 := j_step(0, 0, 1, 0)
  j5 := j_step(1, 1, -1, 0)
  j6 := j_step(0, 1, 1, 0)
  pinclear(J_PIN)
  p4(string("J controls: cog 0 drives 0, worker drives 1, worker drives 0, cog 0 drives 1"), j1, j2, j4, j5)
  p2(string("J measure: worker OUT 1 under cog 0's DIR; cog 0 OUT 1 under the worker's DIR"), j3, j6)
  if j2 == -2 or j4 == -2
    pv(string("J"), string("NO READING, a control's worker did not start"))
  elseif j1 == -3 or j2 == -3 or j4 == -3 or j5 == -3
    pv(string("J"), string("RIG FAIL, a control cog's DIR or OUT read back other than set"))
  elseif j1 <> 0 or j2 <> 1 or j4 <> 0 or j5 <> 1
    pv(string("J"), string("RIG FAIL, a control did not read its level"))
  else
    j_say(string("J worker OUT, cog 0 DIR"), j3)
    j_say(string("J cog 0 OUT, worker DIR"), j6)

PRI j_say(pArm, r)
' Print an arm J verdict.
'
' @param pArm - which way round
' @param r - the pin

  if r == 1
    pv(pArm, string("INDEPENDENT, a cog's OUT reaches the pin while only another cog's DIR is high"))
  elseif r == 0
    pv(pArm, string("GATED, a cog's OUT does not reach the pin without its own DIR"))
  elseif r == -2
    pv(pArm, string("NO READING, step hung: the worker did not start"))
  elseif r == -3
    pv(pArm, string("RIG FAIL, a cog's DIR or OUT read back other than set"))
  else
    pv(pArm, string("OTHER, the three reads differed"))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm K

PRI kx(k) : x
' X of QMUL k,$FFFF_FFFF.
'
' @param k - the multiplier
' @returns x - the low long, -k

  x := -k

PRI ky(k) : y
' Y of QMUL k,$FFFF_FFFF.
'
' @param k - the multiplier
' @returns y - the high long, k - 1

  y := k - 1

PRI arm_k() | ok0, ok1, ok2, ok3, ok4, ctl, a2, b2, a3, b3, a4, b4
' Which read retires a CORDIC result.
'

  ok0 := launch(@k_entry, M_KX4, 0, 0)
  p4(string("K control X stream: X X X X"), rec[R_V], rec[R_V + 1], rec[R_V + 2], rec[R_V + 3])
  ctl := ok0 and rec[R_V] == kx(3) and rec[R_V + 1] == kx(5) and rec[R_V + 2] == kx(7) and rec[R_V + 3] == kx(9)
  ok1 := launch(@k_entry, M_KYX, 0, 0)
  p4(string("K control Y then X: Y X Y X"), rec[R_V], rec[R_V + 1], rec[R_V + 2], rec[R_V + 3])
  ctl := ctl and ok1 and rec[R_V] == ky(3) and rec[R_V + 1] == kx(3) and rec[R_V + 2] == ky(5) and rec[R_V + 3] == kx(5)
  ok2 := launch(@k_entry, M_KXX, 0, 0)
  a2 := rec[R_V]
  b2 := rec[R_V + 1]
  ok3 := launch(@k_entry, M_KXY, 0, 0)
  a3 := rec[R_V]
  b3 := rec[R_V + 1]
  ok4 := launch(@k_entry, M_KYY, 0, 0)
  a4 := rec[R_V]
  b4 := rec[R_V + 1]
  p2(string("K GETQX, GETQX"), a2, b2)
  p2(string("K GETQX, GETQY"), a3, b3)
  p2(string("K GETQY, GETQY"), a4, b4)
  p4(string("K finished: X X, X Y, Y Y, controls"), ok2, ok3, ok4, ctl)
  if not ok0 or not ok1
    pv(string("K"), string("NO READING, a control step hung"))
    return
  if not ctl
    pv(string("K"), string("RIG FAIL, a control stream did not read its results in order"))
    return
  k_say(string("K GETQX then GETQX"), ok2, a2 == kx(3), b2 == kx(5), b2 == kx(3))
  k_say(string("K GETQX then GETQY"), ok3, a3 == kx(3), b3 == ky(5), b3 == ky(3))
  k_say(string("K GETQY then GETQY"), ok4, a4 == ky(3), b4 == ky(5), b4 == ky(3))

PRI k_say(pArm, ok, bFirst, bNext, bSame)
' Print an arm K verdict.
'
' @param pArm - the read pair
' @param ok - the step finished
' @param bFirst - the first read named result 1
' @param bNext - the second read named result 2
' @param bSame - the second read named result 1

  if not ok
    pv(pArm, string("NO READING, step hung"))
  elseif not bFirst
    pv(pArm, string("OTHER, the first read did not name result 1"))
  elseif bNext
    pv(pArm, string("RETIRED, the first read moved on to result 2"))
  elseif bSame
    pv(pArm, string("NOT RETIRED, the second read still names result 1"))
  else
    pv(pArm, string("OTHER, see the raw line"))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm L

PRI arm_l() | ok
' QDIV with a quotient over 32 bits.
'

  ok := launch(@k_entry, M_L, 0, 0)
  p2(string("L control 1000/3: quotient, remainder"), rec[R_V], rec[R_V + 1])
  p2(string("L control {1,0}/4"), rec[R_V + 2], rec[R_V + 3])
  p2(string("L {3,7}/2: true $1_8000_0003 r 1"), rec[R_V + 4], rec[R_V + 5])
  p2(string("L {5,11}/4: true $1_4000_0002 r 3"), rec[R_V + 6], rec[R_V + 7])
  p2(string("L control {$1234_5678,7}/0"), rec[R_V + 8], rec[R_V + 9])
  if not ok
    pv(string("L"), string("NO READING, step hung"))
    return
  if rec[R_V] <> 333 or rec[R_V + 1] <> 1 or rec[R_V + 2] <> $4000_0000 or rec[R_V + 3] <> 0 or rec[R_V + 8] <> !$1234_5678 or rec[R_V + 9] <> 7
    pv(string("L"), string("RIG FAIL, a control quotient or remainder missed"))
    return
  if rec[R_V + 4] == 3 or rec[R_V + 6] == 2
    pv(string("L"), string("RIG FAIL, a quotient is the low long's alone, so the SETQ high long is not shown"))
    return
  if rec[R_V + 4] == $8000_0003 and rec[R_V + 6] == $4000_0002
    pv(string("L quotient"), string("WRAP, both quotients are the low 32 bits of the true quotient"))
  elseif rec[R_V + 4] == $FFFF_FFFF and rec[R_V + 6] == $FFFF_FFFF
    pv(string("L quotient"), string("SATURATE, both quotients are $FFFF_FFFF"))
  else
    pv(string("L quotient"), string("OTHER, see the raw lines"))
  if rec[R_V + 5] == 1 and rec[R_V + 7] == 3
    pv(string("L remainder"), string("TRUE, both remainders are the true remainders"))
  else
    pv(string("L remainder"), string("OTHER, see the raw lines"))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm M

PRI arm_m() | ok, ov, i, bTime, bStale, bZero
' GETQX with nothing pending.  Each read leaves value, clocks, empty flag.
'

  ok := launch(@k_entry, M_M, 0, 0)
  ov := rec[R_V]
  p1(string("M GETCT pair overhead"), ov)
  repeat i from 0 to 1
    p3(string("M pending read: value, clocks, empty flag"), rec[R_V + 1 + i * 6], rec[R_V + 2 + i * 6] - ov, rec[R_V + 3 + i * 6])
    p3(string("M empty read: value, clocks, empty flag"), rec[R_V + 4 + i * 6], rec[R_V + 5 + i * 6] - ov, rec[R_V + 6 + i * 6])
  if not ok
    pv(string("M"), string("NO READING, step hung"))
    return
  if ov <> 2 or rec[R_V + 1] <> kx(3) or rec[R_V + 7] <> kx(5) or rec[R_V + 2] - ov <= 2 or rec[R_V + 8] - ov <= 2 or rec[R_V + 3] <> 0 or rec[R_V + 9] <> 0
    pv(string("M"), string("RIG FAIL, the overhead was not 2 or a pending read did not wait, name its result and leave the flag clear"))
    return
  if rec[R_V + 6] <> 1 or rec[R_V + 12] <> 1
    pv(string("M"), string("RIG FAIL, an empty read did not set the empty flag, so nothing-pending is not shown"))
    return
  bStale := rec[R_V + 4] == kx(3) and rec[R_V + 10] == kx(5)
  bZero := rec[R_V + 4] == 0 and rec[R_V + 10] == 0
  bTime := rec[R_V + 5] - ov == 2 and rec[R_V + 11] - ov == 2
  if bStale
    pv(string("M value"), string("STALE, an empty GETQX returns the last result it read"))
  elseif bZero
    pv(string("M value"), string("ZERO, an empty GETQX returns 0"))
  else
    pv(string("M value"), string("OTHER, see the raw lines"))
  if bTime
    pv(string("M clocks"), string("2, an empty GETQX takes two clocks"))
  else
    pv(string("M clocks"), string("OTHER, see the raw lines"))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm N

PRI arm_n() | ok, ctl, ui, ur, uw, vi, vr, dr, dw, iw
' RDLUT / WRLUT with PTRA expressions.
'

  ok := launch(@k_entry, M_N, @n_hl, @n_hb)
  p1(string("N control LUT[5]"), rec[R_V])
  p3(string("N control hub long: PTRA[2], PTRA++ read, delta"), rec[R_V + 1], rec[R_V + 2], rec[R_V + 3])
  p3(string("N control hub byte: PTRA[2], PTRA++ read, delta"), rec[R_V + 4], rec[R_V + 5], rec[R_V + 6])
  vi := rec[R_V + 7] - LUTBASE
  vr := rec[R_V + 8] - LUTBASE
  dr := rec[R_V + 9]
  dw := rec[R_V + 10]
  iw := rec[R_V + 11]
  p2(string("N RDLUT PTRA[2] with PTRA 8: value, index"), rec[R_V + 7], vi)
  p3(string("N RDLUT PTRA++: value, index, delta"), rec[R_V + 8], vr, dr)
  p2(string("N WRLUT PTRA++: index written, delta"), iw, dw)
  if not ok
    pv(string("N"), string("NO READING, step hung"))
    return
  ctl := rec[R_V] == LUTBASE + 5 and rec[R_V + 1] == $AB00_0002 and rec[R_V + 2] == $AB00_0000 and rec[R_V + 3] == 4
  ctl := ctl and rec[R_V + 4] == $42 and rec[R_V + 5] == $40 and rec[R_V + 6] == 1
  if not ctl
    pv(string("N"), string("RIG FAIL, the LUT contents or a hub pointer control missed"))
    return
  ui := (vi == 10) ? 1 : ((vi == 16) ? 4 : 0)
  ur := (vr == 8 and dr == 1) ? 1 : ((vr == 8 and dr == 4) ? 4 : 0)
  uw := (iw == 8 and dw == 1) ? 1 : ((iw == 8 and dw == 4) ? 4 : 0)
  n_say(string("N RDLUT PTRA[2]"), ui)
  n_say(string("N RDLUT PTRA++"), ur)
  n_say(string("N WRLUT PTRA++"), uw)
  if ui == 1 and ur == 1 and uw == 1
    pv(string("N"), string("LONGS, LUT pointer indexes and updates count LUT longs"))
  elseif ui == 4 and ur == 4 and uw == 4
    pv(string("N"), string("TIMES 4, LUT pointer indexes and updates step by four as RDLONG does"))
  else
    pv(string("N"), string("MIXED, see the lines above"))

PRI n_say(pForm, u)
' Print one arm N form's unit.
'
' @param pForm - the form
' @param u - 1, 4 or 0

  case u
    1:     pv(pForm, string("LONGS"))
    4:     pv(pForm, string("TIMES 4"))
    other: pv(pForm, string("OTHER, see the raw line"))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- arm O

PRI arm_o() | ok, i, nib, dn, up, bDiff, bDown, bUp
' CRCNIB's bit order against four CRCBITs.
'

  ok := launch(@k_entry, M_O, 0, 0)
  bDiff := TRUE
  bDown := TRUE
  bUp := TRUE
  repeat i from 0 to 1
    nib := rec[R_V + i * 3]
    dn := rec[R_V + i * 3 + 1]
    up := rec[R_V + i * 3 + 2]
    p4(string("O data, CRCNIB, CRCBIT Q[31] down, CRCBIT Q[28] up"), lookupz(i: $8000_0000, $D000_0000), nib, dn, up)
    if dn == up
      bDiff := FALSE
    if nib <> dn
      bDown := FALSE
    if nib <> up
      bUp := FALSE
  if not ok
    pv(string("O"), string("NO READING, step hung"))
  elseif not bDiff
    pv(string("O"), string("RIG FAIL, the two CRCBIT orders did not differ"))
  elseif bDown
    pv(string("O"), string("Q[31] FIRST, CRCNIB takes Q[31] down to Q[28]"))
  elseif bUp
    pv(string("O"), string("Q[28] FIRST, CRCNIB takes Q[28] up to Q[31]"))
  else
    pv(string("O"), string("OTHER, see the raw lines"))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- printing

PRI p0(pS)
' Print a hub string.
'
' @param pS - the string

  debug(zstr_(pS))

PRI p1(pS, a)
' Print a hub string and one value.
'
' @param pS - the string
' @param a - the value

  debug(zstr_(pS), " ", uhex_long_(a))

PRI p2(pS, a, b)
' Print a hub string and two values.
'
' @param pS - the string
' @param a - first value
' @param b - second value

  debug(zstr_(pS), " ", uhex_long_(a), " ", uhex_long_(b))

PRI p3(pS, a, b, c)
' Print a hub string and three values.
'
' @param pS - the string
' @param a - first value
' @param b - second value
' @param c - third value

  debug(zstr_(pS), " ", uhex_long_(a), " ", uhex_long_(b), " ", uhex_long_(c))

PRI p4(pS, a, b, c, d)
' Print a hub string and four values.
'
' @param pS - the string
' @param a - first value
' @param b - second value
' @param c - third value
' @param d - fourth value

  debug(zstr_(pS), " ", uhex_long_(a), " ", uhex_long_(b), " ", uhex_long_(c), " ", uhex_long_(d))

PRI pv(pArm, pText)
' Print one verdict line.
'
' @param pArm - the arm
' @param pText - the verdict

  debug("VERDICT ", zstr_(pArm), ": ", zstr_(pText))

PRI pv2(pArm, pCls, pText, v)
' Print one verdict line for a class, with its reading.
'
' @param pArm - the arm and scenario
' @param pCls - the class
' @param pText - the verdict
' @param v - the reading

  debug("VERDICT ", zstr_(pArm), " ", zstr_(pCls), ": ", zstr_(pText), " ", uhex_long_(v))

DAT ' ---- arm I: one image is the reader and the dirtier ----
                alignl
                org     0
i_r00           add     i_skm, #1               ' $000 skip detector
                add     i_skm, #2
                add     i_skm, #4
                add     i_skm, #8
                add     i_skm, #16
                add     i_skm, #32
                add     i_skm, #64
                add     i_skm, #128             ' $007
                wrc     i_cv
                wrz     i_zv
                mov     i_pav, pa
                mov     i_pbv, pb
                mov     i_qv, #0
                muxq    i_qv, i_ones
                nop
i_repsite       nop                             ' $00F the dirtier writes a REP here
i_repblk        add     i_rpc, #1               ' $010 REP detector
                wrlong  i_rpc, ptra[IR_BEAT]    ' $011 a held REP shows a moving count
                nop                             ' $012
                mov     i_dirv, dira
                mov     i_outv, outa
                rdlut   i_lutv, #I_LS
                pop     i_st0
                pop     i_st1
                pop     i_st2
                pop     i_st3
                pop     i_st4
                pop     i_st5
                pop     i_st6
                pop     i_st7
                pollct1                 wc      ' clears the flag; C = already fired
                wrc     i_ct0
                getct   i_ctst
.w              pollct1                 wc
        if_c    jmp     #.hit
                getct   i_t
                sub     i_t, i_ctst
                cmp     i_t, i_win      wc
        if_c    jmp     #.w
                mov     i_ctfl, #0
                mov     i_ctf, #0
                jmp     #.chk
.hit            getct   i_ctf
                mov     i_ctfl, #1
.chk            tjnz    i_entered, #i_report    ' a plain jump back in reports
                mov     i_entered, #1
                rdlong  i_mode, ptra[R_MODE]
                tjz     i_mode, #i_report       ' mode 0: a reader
                rdlong  i_rec2, ptra[R_P1]
                rdlong  i_img, ptra[R_P2]
                mov     i_var, i_mode
                shr     i_var, #2
                and     i_mode, #3
                cmp     i_var, #V_PAS   wz
        if_z    jmp     #i_dp
                cmp     i_var, #V_SKIP  wz
        if_z    jmp     #i_ds
                jmp     #i_dr

i_report        mov     i_p, ptra
                add     i_p, #I_CAP * 4
                setq    #I_NCAP - 1
                wrlong  i_skm, i_p
                wrlong  i_donev, ptra
                mov     dira, #0
                jmp     #$

' passive dirty state
i_dp            mov     outa, #D_OUT
                mov     dira, #D_DIR
                push    i_s1
                push    i_s2
                push    i_s3
                push    i_s4
                push    i_s5
                push    i_s6
                push    i_s7
                push    i_s8
                wrlut   i_lutd, #I_LS
                mov     pa, i_pad
                mov     pb, i_pbd
                getct   i_t
                addct1  i_t, i_ctdel
                wrlong  i_t, ptra[I_TD]
                cmp     i_mode, #SC_SELF    wz
        if_z    jmp     #.self
                cmp     i_mode, #SC_JMP     wz
        if_z    jmp     #.jmp
                setq    i_qd                    ' running or stopped: hold here
                modcz   _set, _set      wcz
                wrlong  #1, ptra[I_READY]
                jmp     #$
.self           modcz   _set, _set      wcz
                wrlong  #1, ptra[I_READY]
                cogid   i_id
                setq    i_rec2
                coginit i_id, i_img
.jmp            mov     i_skm, #0
                mov     i_rpc, #0
                setq    i_qd
                modcz   _set, _set      wcz
                wrlong  #1, ptra[I_READY]
                jmp     #\i_r00

' skip pattern held while the COGINIT arrives
i_ds            mov     i_skm, #0
                cmp     i_mode, #SC_SELF    wz
        if_z    jmp     #.self
                cmp     i_mode, #SC_JMP     wz
        if_z    jmp     #.jmp
                wrlong  #1, ptra[I_READY]
.loop           skip    i_spat                  ' bit 2 and bits 7..31 pending
                add     i_beat, #1              ' bit 0: the loop is running
                wrlong  i_beat, ptra[IR_BEAT]    ' bit 1
                add     i_leak, #1              ' bit 2: runs only if the pattern is gone
                wrlong  i_leak, ptra[IR_LEAK]    ' bit 3
                jmp     #.loop                  ' bit 4
                long    0[32]
                jmp     #.loop
.self           wrlong  #1, ptra[I_READY]
                cogid   i_id
                skip    i_spself                ' bit 0 and bits 4..31 pending
                add     i_leak, #1              ' bit 0: runs only if the pattern is gone
                wrlong  i_leak, ptra[IR_LEAK]    ' bit 1
                setq    i_rec2                  ' bit 2
                coginit i_id, i_img             ' bit 3
.jmp            wrlong  #1, ptra[I_READY]
                skip    i_spjmp                 ' the JMP runs, eight pending 1s
                jmp     #\i_r00

' REP held while the COGINIT arrives
i_dr            mov     i_rpc, #0
                cmp     i_mode, #SC_SELF    wz
        if_z    jmp     #.self
                mov     i_repsite, i_reptpl
                cmp     i_mode, #SC_JMP     wz
        if_z    mov     i_rcnt, #K_CTL
        if_nz   mov     i_rcnt, i_rbig
                wrlong  #1, ptra[I_READY]
                jmp     #i_repsite
.self           mov     i_repsite, i_rep5tpl    ' REP #5 over $010..$014
                mov     i_repblk + 2, i_selft0  ' $012: CMP i_rpc,#2 WZ
                mov     i_repblk + 3, i_selft1  ' $013: IF_Z SETQ
                mov     i_repblk + 4, i_selft2  ' $014: IF_Z COGINIT
                mov     i_rcnt, #K_SELF
                cogid   i_id
                wrlong  #1, ptra[I_READY]
                jmp     #i_repsite              ' pass 1 writes 1; only REP brings pass 2, which writes 2 and restarts

i_skm           long    0                       ' i_skm .. i_ctst: the captures, in order
i_cv            long    0
i_zv            long    0
i_pav           long    0
i_pbv           long    0
i_qv            long    0
i_rpc           long    0
i_dirv          long    0
i_outv          long    0
i_lutv          long    0
i_st0           long    0
i_st1           long    0
i_st2           long    0
i_st3           long    0
i_st4           long    0
i_st5           long    0
i_st6           long    0
i_st7           long    0
i_ct0           long    0
i_ctfl          long    0
i_ctf           long    0
i_ctst          long    0
i_entered       long    0
i_mode          long    0
i_var           long    0
i_t             long    0
i_p             long    0
i_id            long    0
i_rec2          long    0
i_img           long    0
i_rcnt          long    0
i_ones          long    $FFFF_FFFF
i_win           long    CT_WIN
i_ctdel         long    CT_DEL
i_s1            long    D_STK + 1
i_s2            long    D_STK + 2
i_s3            long    D_STK + 3
i_s4            long    D_STK + 4
i_s5            long    D_STK + 5
i_s6            long    D_STK + 6
i_s7            long    D_STK + 7
i_s8            long    D_STK + 8
i_lutd          long    D_LUT
i_pad           long    D_PA
i_pbd           long    D_PB
i_qd            long    D_Q
i_spat          long    $FFFF_FF84
i_spself        long    $FFFF_FFF1
i_beat          long    0
i_leak          long    0
i_spjmp         long    $0000_01FE
i_rbig          long    K_BIG
i_donev         long    DONE_V
i_reptpl        rep     #3, i_rcnt              ' templates, written into $00F and $012..$014
i_rep5tpl       rep     #5, i_rcnt
i_selft0        cmp     i_rpc, #2       wz
i_selft1 if_z   setq    i_rec2
i_selft2 if_z   coginit i_id, i_img
                long    0[$1F6 - $]
                long    IMG_PA, IMG_PB          ' loaded into PA and PB

DAT ' ---- arm J worker ----
                alignl
                org     0
j_entry         rdlong  j_d, ptra[R_P1]
                rdlong  j_o, ptra[R_P2]
                testb   j_o, #0         wc
                outc    #J_PIN
                testb   j_d, #0         wc
                dirc    #J_PIN
                testb   dira, #J_PIN    wc      ' read back DIR | OUT << 1
                wrc     j_s
                testb   outa, #J_PIN    wc
                bitc    j_s, #1
                wrlong  j_s, ptra[J_STATE]
                wrlong  #1, ptra[J_READY]
                jmp     #$
j_d             long    0
j_o             long    0
j_s             long    0

DAT ' ---- arms K to O worker ----
                alignl
                org     0
k_entry         mov     k_rec, ptra
                mov     k_wp, ptra
                add     k_wp, #R_V * 4
                rdlong  k_mode, ptra[R_MODE]
                rdlong  k_p1, ptra[R_P1]
                rdlong  k_p2, ptra[R_P2]
                cmp     k_mode, #M_KX4  wz
        if_z    jmp     #k_x4
                cmp     k_mode, #M_KYX  wz
        if_z    jmp     #k_yx
                cmp     k_mode, #M_KXX  wz
        if_z    jmp     #k_xx
                cmp     k_mode, #M_KXY  wz
        if_z    jmp     #k_xy
                cmp     k_mode, #M_KYY  wz
        if_z    jmp     #k_yy
                cmp     k_mode, #M_L    wz
        if_z    jmp     #k_l
                cmp     k_mode, #M_M    wz
        if_z    jmp     #k_m
                cmp     k_mode, #M_N    wz
        if_z    jmp     #k_n
                cmp     k_mode, #M_O    wz
        if_z    jmp     #k_o
                jmp     #k_done

' arm K
k_x4            qmul    k_k3, k_ones
                qmul    k_k5, k_ones
                qmul    k_k7, k_ones
                qmul    k_k9, k_ones
                getqx   k_a
                getqx   k_b
                getqx   k_c
                getqx   k_d
                jmp     #k_put4
k_yx            qmul    k_k3, k_ones
                qmul    k_k5, k_ones
                getqy   k_a
                getqx   k_b
                getqy   k_c
                getqx   k_d
                jmp     #k_put4
k_xx            qmul    k_k3, k_ones
                qmul    k_k5, k_ones
                getqx   k_a
                getqx   k_b
                jmp     #k_put2
k_xy            qmul    k_k3, k_ones
                qmul    k_k5, k_ones
                getqx   k_a
                getqy   k_b
                jmp     #k_put2
k_yy            qmul    k_k3, k_ones
                qmul    k_k5, k_ones
                getqy   k_a
                getqy   k_b
                jmp     #k_put2

k_put4          mov     k_v, k_a
                call    #k_put
                mov     k_v, k_b
                call    #k_put
                mov     k_v, k_c
                call    #k_put
                mov     k_v, k_d
                call    #k_put
                jmp     #k_drain
k_put2          mov     k_v, k_a
                call    #k_put
                mov     k_v, k_b
                call    #k_put
k_drain         waitx   #100                    ' leave nothing pending for the next step
                pollqmt                 wc
                mov     k_n8, #8
.d              getqx   k_t
                jqmt    #k_done
                djnz    k_n8, #.d
                jmp     #k_done

k_put           wrlong  k_v, k_wp
        _ret_   add     k_wp, #4

' arm L
k_l             qdiv    k_1000, #3              ' control: 333 r 1
                call    #k_qput
                setq    #1
                qdiv    k_0, #4                 ' control: {1,0}/4
                call    #k_qput
                setq    #3
                qdiv    k_7, #2                 ' {3,7}/2; without the SETQ it would be 3 r 1
                call    #k_qput
                setq    #5
                qdiv    k_11, #4                ' {5,11}/4; without the SETQ it would be 2 r 3
                call    #k_qput
                setq    k_hi
                qdiv    k_7, #0                 ' control: divide by zero
                call    #k_qput
                jmp     #k_done

k_qput          getqx   k_v
                call    #k_put
                getqy   k_v
                jmp     #k_put

' arm M
k_m             getct   k_t0
                getct   k_t1                    ' control: the pair's overhead
                mov     k_v, k_t1
                sub     k_v, k_t0
                call    #k_put
                pollqmt                 wc
                qmul    k_k3, k_ones
                call    #k_mread                ' pending
                call    #k_mread                ' empty
                qmul    k_k5, k_ones
                call    #k_mread                ' pending
                call    #k_mread                ' empty
                jmp     #k_done

k_mread         getct   k_t0
                getqx   k_v
                getct   k_t1
                pollqmt                 wc      ' C = the empty flag
                wrc     k_q
                call    #k_put
                mov     k_v, k_t1
                sub     k_v, k_t0
                call    #k_put
                mov     k_v, k_q
                jmp     #k_put

' arm N
k_n             mov     k_i, #0
                rep     @.f, #32
                mov     k_t, k_i
                or      k_t, k_lutb
                wrlut   k_t, k_i
                add     k_i, #1
.f              rdlut   k_v, #5                 ' control: known contents
                call    #k_put
                mov     ptra, k_p1              ' control: hub longs
                rdlong  k_v, ptra[2]
                call    #k_put
                rdlong  k_v, ptra++
                call    #k_put
                mov     k_v, ptra
                sub     k_v, k_p1
                call    #k_put
                mov     ptra, k_p2              ' control: hub bytes
                rdbyte  k_v, ptra[2]
                call    #k_put
                rdbyte  k_v, ptra++
                call    #k_put
                mov     k_v, ptra
                sub     k_v, k_p2
                call    #k_put
                mov     ptra, #8
                rdlut   k_v, ptra[2]            ' indexed read
                call    #k_put
                mov     ptra, #8
                rdlut   k_v, ptra++             ' post-increment read
                call    #k_put
                mov     k_v, ptra
                sub     k_v, #8
                call    #k_put
                mov     ptra, #8
                wrlut   k_mark, ptra++          ' post-increment write
                mov     k_v, ptra
                sub     k_v, #8
                call    #k_put
                mov     k_i, #0
                neg     k_w, #1
.s              rdlut   k_t, k_i                ' where the mark landed
                cmp     k_t, k_mark     wz
        if_z    mov     k_w, k_i
                add     k_i, #1
                cmp     k_i, #32        wc
        if_c    jmp     #.s
                mov     k_v, k_w
                call    #k_put
                mov     ptra, k_rec
                jmp     #k_done

' arm O
k_o             mov     k_dat, k_d1
                call    #k_crc
                mov     k_dat, k_d2
                call    #k_crc
                jmp     #k_done

k_crc           mov     k_v, #0
                setq    k_dat
                crcnib  k_v, #$8C
                call    #k_put
                mov     k_v, #0                 ' Q[31] down
                testb   k_dat, #31      wc
                crcbit  k_v, #$8C
                testb   k_dat, #30      wc
                crcbit  k_v, #$8C
                testb   k_dat, #29      wc
                crcbit  k_v, #$8C
                testb   k_dat, #28      wc
                crcbit  k_v, #$8C
                call    #k_put
                mov     k_v, #0                 ' Q[28] up
                testb   k_dat, #28      wc
                crcbit  k_v, #$8C
                testb   k_dat, #29      wc
                crcbit  k_v, #$8C
                testb   k_dat, #30      wc
                crcbit  k_v, #$8C
                testb   k_dat, #31      wc
                crcbit  k_v, #$8C
                jmp     #k_put

k_done          mov     ptra, k_rec
                wrlong  k_donev, ptra
                jmp     #$

k_rec           long    0
k_wp            long    0
k_mode          long    0
k_p1            long    0
k_p2            long    0
k_a             long    0
k_b             long    0
k_c             long    0
k_d             long    0
k_v             long    0
k_t             long    0
k_t0            long    0
k_t1            long    0
k_q             long    0
k_n8            long    0
k_i             long    0
k_w             long    0
k_dat           long    0
k_k3            long    3
k_k5            long    5
k_k7            long    7
k_k9            long    9
k_ones          long    $FFFF_FFFF
k_0             long    0
k_1             long    1
k_3             long    3
k_7             long    7
k_11            long    11
k_1000          long    1000
k_hi            long    $1234_5678
k_lutb          long    LUTBASE
k_mark          long    N_MARK
k_d1            long    $8000_0000
k_d2            long    $D000_0000
k_donev         long    DONE_V

DAT ' ---- hub data ----
                orgh
                alignl
sSurv           byte    "SURVIVES", 0
                alignl
n_hl            long    $AB00_0000, $AB00_0001, $AB00_0002, $AB00_0003
n_hb            byte    $40, $41, $42, $43, $44, $45, $46, $47
